From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_pr_fixes_use_quaran <>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:43:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] os/mm: Stop over-aligning the poisoned window

The window started at MM_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE), which rounds up
to the 16 byte allocator granule. It only has to be 32-bit aligned, and
SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE is a multiple of four in every supported
configuration, so the granule rounding was giving away detection
coverage for nothing.

On the common configuration with CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_HEAPINFO enabled the
free node is 24 bytes and the window started at 32, so eight bytes of
user data went unchecked. Worse, a 32 byte chunk got no coverage at
all, which is every freed allocation of 16 bytes or less. Rounding to a
whole word instead recovers those bytes and gives small chunks a
window, so writes the detector previously walked straight past are now
reported.

Also correct the Kconfig help, which implied that a write into the
region that still cannot be covered is caught by
DEBUGASSERT_MM_FREE_NODE. That macro only checks blink for NULL, so a
write of any other value, or a write to flink, is not detected. State
the limit plainly rather than implying cover which does not exist.
---
 os/Kconfig.debug           |  8 ++++++++
 os/include/tinyara/mm/mm.h |  9 ++++++++-
 os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c     | 15 +++++++++------
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/os/Kconfig.debug b/os/Kconfig.debug
index 17b9fe4a..79dc55d1 100644
--- a/os/Kconfig.debug
+++ b/os/Kconfig.debug
@@ -799,6 +799,14 @@ config DEBUG_MM_UAF
 		chunk is handed out by malloc. A mismatch means somebody wrote into
 		the chunk after it was freed (use-after-free).
 
+		Not covered: the free node bookkeeping at the start of the user data,
+		from offset 0 up to SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE. The allocator reuses that
+		region for flink, blink and the free debug info while the chunk is on
+		the free list, so it cannot hold the pattern. A write there corrupts
+		the free list; DEBUGASSERT_MM_FREE_NODE catches the case where blink
+		is left NULL, but a write of any other value, or a write to flink, is
+		not detected.
+
 if DEBUG_MM_UAF
 
 config DEBUG_MM_UAF_POISON_SIZE
diff --git a/os/include/tinyara/mm/mm.h b/os/include/tinyara/mm/mm.h
index 48fd8eb4..8cddd18e 100644
--- a/os/include/tinyara/mm/mm.h
+++ b/os/include/tinyara/mm/mm.h
@@ -173,7 +173,14 @@
 #define MM_REMAINDER_FREE_CALL_PID 	((pid_t)-1)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF
-#define MM_UAF_PATTERN	0xA5A5A5A5
+#define MM_UAF_PATTERN	0xA5A5A5A5u
+
+/* Round up to a whole poison word. The window only has to be 32-bit aligned,
+ * so rounding to the allocator granule with MM_ALIGN_UP() would give away
+ * coverage for nothing.
+ */
+
+#define MM_UAF_ALIGN_UP(a)	(((a) + (sizeof(uint32_t) - 1)) & ~(sizeof(uint32_t) - 1))
 #endif
 
 /****************************************************************************
diff --git a/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c b/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
index c81418c9..e6127c5b 100644
--- a/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
+++ b/os/mm/mm_heap/mm_uaf.c
@@ -56,10 +56,13 @@
  *   bookkeeping fields (flink/blink and the free debug info) which the
  *   allocator itself keeps using while the chunk sits in the free list.
  *
- *   Those fields are skipped by MM_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE), the same
- *   granule alignment the allocator applies to every other offset. Since a
- *   node address is always a multiple of sizeof(uint32_t), that keeps the
- *   pattern accessible with aligned 32-bit reads and writes.
+ *   Those fields end at SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE, which is a multiple of four in
+ *   every supported configuration, so rounding that up to a whole word is all
+ *   that is needed to keep the pattern reachable with aligned 32-bit accesses.
+ *   Rounding up to the allocator granule instead, as MM_ALIGN_UP() does,
+ *   pushes the window a further eight bytes into the chunk on the common
+ *   HEAPINFO configuration and leaves a 32 byte chunk with no coverage at
+ *   all.
  *
  *   The size is clamped to CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF_POISON_SIZE and truncated to
  *   whole words, so nothing is ever written past the end of the chunk.
@@ -72,7 +75,7 @@
 
 static size_t mm_uaf_area(struct mm_freenode_s *node, uint32_t **poison)
 {
-	size_t offset = MM_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE);
+	size_t offset = MM_UAF_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE);
 	size_t nbytes;
 
 	if (node->size <= offset) {
@@ -162,7 +165,7 @@ void mm_uaf_verify(struct mm_freenode_s *node)
 	 * the chunk as the bound allows.
 	 */
 
-	dumpsize = MM_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE) + nwords * sizeof(uint32_t);
+	dumpsize = MM_UAF_ALIGN_UP(SIZEOF_MM_FREENODE) + nwords * sizeof(uint32_t);
 	if (dumpsize < MM_UAF_DUMP_MAX) {
 		dumpsize = MM_UAF_DUMP_MAX;
 	}
